1
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:14,470
Four numbers. Five sources. They disagree, and nothing says so.

2
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:24,210
The bar stops where the agreement stops.

3
00:00:24,490 --> 00:00:34,010
The ordinary rule files the wrong number, silently.

4
00:00:34,290 --> 00:00:47,650
Every number pinned to its exact line, and to a moment in time.

5
00:00:47,930 --> 00:00:58,200
No source? It cannot be decided. Only attested, by name.

6
00:00:58,480 --> 00:01:08,000
9 roles, 40 steps, 3 model companies.

7
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:16,830
Half the run contains no model. A model cannot check a model.

8
00:01:17,110 --> 00:01:23,130
A named person decides. A second person signs off.

9
00:01:23,410 --> 00:01:27,630
Sealed. Change one byte and the chain breaks.

10
00:01:27,910 --> 00:01:38,800
24 of 24 planted failures caught. 0 silent picks.

11
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:50,100
All data synthetic. What is missing, only access can fix.
